        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0437" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg329"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 154.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your dispatch
                    No. 70 of the 26th ultimo, I have to inform you that your course in declining to
                    issue a passport to Mr. Fielder J. Hiss is approved by the Department. Your
                    statements show conclusively that he has voluntarily transferred his domicil to
                    England, that he does so permanently, and that he has no intention to resume
                    here the resident obligations of citizenship. He does this, not in
                    representation of any American interest, but to identify himself with British
                    interests. These facts completely negative the applicants’ right to an American
                    passport.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
